{
  "kanji": "文",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 文\ntitle: sentence, writing\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-1, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 4\nradical: 文\nradicalNumber: 67\nonyomi: [ブン, モン]\nkunyomi: [ふみ, あや]\ndistractors: [父, 六, 大]\n---\n\n# 文 — sentence, writing\n\n**Strokes:** 4 · **Key (radical):** 文 (no. 67) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n文 concerns sentences and written composition. It also appears in words about culture and the literary arts.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture the crossing lower strokes as a pen moving across a page beneath the top line. This remembers the modern outline; it is not a reconstruction of an ancient picture.\n\n## Readings\n\nThis table is selective; metadata preserves all source on/kun readings.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ブン | on | [作文](../words/作文.md) さくぶん (composition), 文法 ぶんぽう (grammar) |\n| ふみ | kun | 文 ふみ (letter; formal or literary wording) |\n| あや | kun | 文 あや (pattern; design), 言葉のあや (a figure of speech), usually written 言葉の綾 |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [作文](../words/作文.md) さくぶん — composition, essay writing\n- 文法 ぶんぽう — grammar\n- 文章 ぶんしょう — a piece of writing, prose\n- 文字 もじ — written character\n- 文化 ぶんか — culture\n\n## Notes\n\nLearn 文字 as もじ; it is not read ぶんじ. The readings in complete words can differ from the most familiar reading of each character.\n\n[字](字.md) often concerns an individual written character, while 文 often concerns a sentence or writing. [父](父.md) has two separate strokes above the crossing strokes; [六](六.md) has a similar top to 文 but does not cross its two lower strokes.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-08 (EDRDG; [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)).\n",
